# 1. Purpose

This Technical Requirements Document defines the complete technical architecture, technology choices, development conventions, APIs, data models, security approach, external services, project structure, workflows, and implementation rules for the **Quantum Care** web application.

The purpose of this document is to remove technical ambiguity for the development/coding agent.

The coding agent must treat this document as the **technical baseline** and should not independently replace the chosen technologies or introduce unnecessary alternatives.

The original problem statement requires a patient-facing system that can capture structured medical history, digitize existing medical documents, create a physician-ready summary, support multilingual/accessible interaction, detect red flags, and eventually integrate with hospital systems and ABDM.

---

# 2. Current Technical Scope

The first implementation is **WEB ONLY**.

The web application will contain:

```text
Quantum Care
│
├── Patient Web Application
├── Doctor Web Dashboard
└── Admin Web Dashboard
```

The system must be architected so a future kiosk can use the same backend without requiring a new database or duplicated business logic.

Future architecture:

```text
Patient Web
Doctor Web
Admin Web
Hospital Kiosk
      │
      ▼
Quantum Care API
      │
      ▼
MongoDB + Services
```

