# 50. AI Uses

AI is allowed to:

* understand natural patient speech,
* convert patient language into structured text,
* generate adaptive questions,
* structure history,
* summarize information,
* extract clinical entities,
* identify predefined red-flag concepts.

AI is not allowed to:

* make the final diagnosis,
* autonomously prescribe,
* alter verified doctor records,
* fabricate missing information,
* create unsupported patient facts.

---

# 51. AI Question Engine

Use a hybrid system:

```text
Clinical rules
+
Structured questionnaire
+
LLM natural-language generation
```

The rules determine:

* what information is required,
* which sections must be completed,
* which branches are allowed,
* when the interview can finish,
* which predefined red flags matter.

The AI generates the natural conversational wording.

This is more controllable than letting the LLM run the entire medical interview with unrestricted autonomy.

---

# 52. AI Question Response Schema

The AI must return structured JSON:

```json
{
  "questionId": "q_123",
  "section": "HPI",
  "type": "SINGLE_SELECT",
  "question": "When did the pain start?",
  "options": [
    "Today",
    "Yesterday",
    "2-3 days ago",
    "More than a week ago",
    "I don't know"
  ],
  "allowVoice": true,
  "required": true
}
```

Frontend renders the question.

The AI must never generate HTML or React code.

