                         |
       +-----------------+-----------------+
       |                 |                 |
    Patient Web      Doctor Web        Admin Web
       |                 |                 |
       +-----------------+-----------------+
                         |
                    REST API
                         |
                  Node + Express
                         |
       +-----------------+------------------+
       |                 |                  |
    MongoDB        Service Layer       Providers
       |                 |                  |
       |                 |        +---------+---------+
       |                 |        |         |         |
       |                 |      OpenAI    OCR      Maps
       |                 |                  |
       |                 |              Local Files
       |                 |
       +-----------------+
```

Every major external dependency is behind a provider/service boundary.

That means when the prototype becomes a real application, we can replace:

```text
Local MongoDB → Cloud MongoDB
Local files → S3
Prototype auth → OTP/ABHA
No payment → Razorpay
OpenStreetMap → Google Maps if required
Prototype OCR → advanced medical OCR
OpenAI configuration → production AI configuration
Web only → Web + Kiosk
```

without rewriting Quantum Care's core clinical workflow.

The web-first approach also directly supports the original problem's intended patient journey of structured history capture, document digitization, summary generation, and physician review before consultation.
